<title>USA: U.S. power output falls 2.3 pct vs. year ago--EEI.</title>
<headline>U.S. power output falls 2.3 pct vs. year ago--EEI.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity deliveries in the continental U.S. totaled 65,741 gigawatt hours (GWh) for the week ended January 11, down 2.3 percent from the same period in 1996, the Edison Electric Institute (EEI) said.</p>
<p>The amount of weekly power supplied to the southeastern U.S. fell the most, down 9.4 percent to 15,772 GWh, EEI said.</p>
<p>Power output in the Rocky Mountain region bucked the trend, moving up 10.4 percent to 3,298 GWh.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
